<article class="env-lemma" id="08IZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08IZ">Lemma <span data-tag="08IZ">110.62.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X}$ be an algebraic stack. If $\mathcal{F}_ n$ is a collection of locally quasi-coherent sheaves with the flat base change property on $\mathcal{X}$, then $\oplus _ n \mathcal{F}_ n[n] \to \prod _ n \mathcal{F}_ n[n]$ is an isomorphism in $D(\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because by Lemma <a href="/tag/08IY" data-tag="08IY">110.62.1</a> we see that the direct sum is isomorphic to the product. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>